rrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> If you're interested, we've got like 6-7 pages of discussion <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483464#post1483464\">here</a> including an awesome education on jewish iconography by Heavy Arms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks. Didn't realise the book was out before I got the mail by drivethru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T10:13:22-07:00","id":1488183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488181#post1488181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thanks. Didn't realise the book was out before I got the mail by drivethru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Renegade likes to keep their books private for a while. I guess for promotion/sales? It is a bit weird.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T10:56:20-07:00","id":1488187,"title":"","content":"Wishing for an H20 instead (which will never come).<br /> <br /> I think this book has quietly crawled into a dark corner and died. There was initial excitement online, then it was announced there were no ties to OG HTR, and it became tumbleweed. <br /> <br /> I've seen a few threads start and fizzle out quickly. Maybe this isn't the best place for fans of H5, though -- maybe they congregate on Renegade forums or something?<br /> <br /> Both the threads I've seen that were very long were mostly people trying to work out who it was appealing to, with half a dozen liking it, and one or two zealously defending it (to the point that they were glossing over racism and other stuff which felt icky). <br /> <br /> Of course, such threads also threatened to tip into edition wars a couple of times, which got uncomfortable, but in the end, they turned out okay and nobody got hurt (I hope).<br /> <br /> I think some people will use the book for its refinements of the V5 system (Drive Fields could be applied to vampires to make Hunger add bonuses to certain in-theme actions, thereby replacing both Blood Surge and Discipline dice bonuses, for example), some will use it as a resource for NPCs for V5 (but even then, it's quite thin on the ground), and some will use it for ST-lite one-shots. But I can't see it gaining the same passionate fanbase as the HTR of yore.<br /> <br /> However, maybe we'll see HTR stuff on STV that resurrects the Imbued, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T12:03:49-07:00","id":1488189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488187#post1488187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, maybe we'll see HTR stuff on STV that resurrects the Imbued, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as the most likely possibility. Writers who create for Storyteller's Vault have been doing the heavy lifting for some time now, and deserve every penny they make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T14:01:00-07:00","id":1488208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488154#post1488154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it succesful in that? I've only scan read it and found it underwritten.</div> </div> </div> </div>From who's perspective?<br /> <br /> For me, as someone that's been playing RPGs for what's approaching three decades now, and for whom VtDA 2e was my second RPG, H5 didn't do a great job of things because it barely feels like the creative team learned anything in ~25 years since that book was published.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, despite all those flaws... much younger me still managed to find out how much gaming there is, and how much I love the WoD, from those books. That younger me didn't care much for the oD&amp;D grognard types droning on about how VtM wasn't doing things right.<br /> <br /> Most people on this forum (and really most RPG forums) are not in the target audience of &quot;trying their first RPG after D&amp;D 5e&quot; to really say if it H5 is good enough for that audience. We can see all the ways it will let that audience down in the future... largely because we've been there in our own ways in the past. But lots of us still love the warty old books, even knowing their flaws all too well, and that nostalgia is a hell of a drug once you get hooked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488189#post1488189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This strikes me as the most likely possibility. Writers who create for Storyteller's Vault have been doing the heavy lifting for some time now, and deserve every penny they make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly they deserve more of the pennies Paradox is making off their backs too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T22:02:35-07:00","id":1488243,"title":"","content":"Boring, uninspired and lacking outside of art style, which is decent. It's basically a diluted version of Tier 1 Hunters of HtV or a new Hunter from Hunters Hunted using the name of the Reckoning to get a sales boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T22:11:22-07:00","id":1488244,"title":"","content":"Also, while the art is, from the decent selection I've seen, is actually really good... but still has the same exact problem HtR 1e had: the art seems detached from what H5 is trying to be and leans into the action oriented monster hunters that regularly fight toe-to-toe with the creatures of the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T22:46:09-07:00","id":1488245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488208#post1488208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From who's perspective?<br /> <br /> For me, as someone that's been playing RPGs for what's approaching three decades now, and for whom VtDA 2e was my second RPG, H5 didn't do a great job of things because it barely feels like the creative team learned anything in ~25 years since that book was published.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, despite all those flaws... much younger me still managed to find out how much gaming there is, and how much I love the WoD, from those books. That younger me didn't care much for the oD&amp;D grognard types droning on about how VtM wasn't doing things right.<br /> <br /> Most people on this forum (and really most RPG forums) are not in the target audience of &amp;quot;trying their first RPG after D&amp;D 5e&amp;quot; to really say if it H5 is good enough for that audience. We can see all the ways it will let that audience down in the future... largely because we've been there in our own ways in the past. But lots of us still love the warty old books, even knowing their flaws all too well, and that nostalgia is a hell of a drug once you get hooked.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Frankly they deserve more of the pennies Paradox is making off their backs too.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true. But one thing that benefited the books in the 90s was that they dripped with mood and the setting felt really rich, even when they hadn't fully fleshed everything out yet. H5 intentionally skimps on the setting, so I can't see people getting hooked enough to become nostalgic later on either.<br /> <br /> Maybe different people will get drawn in for different reasons, and that cover is appealing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T04:17:40-07:00","id":1488252,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest killer to any success with the &quot;my 2nd TTRPG&quot; crowd? Almost $40 for the pdf.<br /> <br /> While, in general, I think RPG pdfs are undervalued and the industry should normalize higher price points for them, that's a huge bar for entry compared to other options. A few bucks more than your main competitors is one thing. This is going to be $10-15 more than most similar products (many of which are giving you more bang for your buck like more thorough antagonist creation systems), and there's no discount for a PoD + pdf combo to help entice people to accept a higher base price or something similar.<br /> <br /> Considering the lack of audience among older games already familiar with the breadth of options in the hunter genre, who are also more likely to be financially well off and would be more like to spend if you tickled their nostalgia a bit more (making the Driven capable of a true Imbued style of play, or not creating an artificial divide between the Driven and orgs so HH could feel appealed to), this feels like a very large issue for a product that's going to rely so much of first time buyers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T14:20:39-07:00","id":1488283,"title":"","content":"Is there a chance the Imbued were retconned out because of copyright issues? <br /> <br /> I mean, apparently, it was considered canon that the messengers were The Scarlett Emperess and the Ebon Dragon. Do Renegade studios have permission to use those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T15:16:57-07:00","id":1488285,"title":"","content":"Paradox owns both the WoD and Exalted, so if that was possibly an issue... it wouldn't be. They'd essentially be suing themselves.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that the two Ministers (not the Heralds/Messengers) were established as beings in the WoD during 2e, well before Exalted was created. HtR 1e used existing canon beings that predated Exalted (even if she was the Scarlett Phoenix originally) because of the initial idea of linking the WoD and Exalted even if that was dropped before anything but an ad went to print.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T16:56:51-07:00","id":1488291,"title":"","content":"as someone who didn't care for the first edition (and generally found the imbued to be... silly, at best) i've been pleasantly surprised by it but i can't see it carrying a long game the way V5 can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T23:26:40-07:00","id":1488323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488291#post1488291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as someone who didn't care for the first edition (and generally found the imbued to be... silly, at best) i've been pleasantly surprised by it but i can't see it carrying a long game the way V5 can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind sharing what appeals to you about the book? Is there anything you'd like them to keep the same/change in future books?<br /> <br /> I think it will be useful in helping the H5-curious figure out whether the book is going to be right for them. I also, selfishly, want WoD books to do well and bring loads of new players in, because even if I don't like some of the stuff 5e does, it does mean we're more likely to keep seeing new books come out for our favourite games (and I am a sucker for buying books, even if I'll never use them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T08:07:28-07:00","id":1488360,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Having looked at the book and given it a quick overview I personally mostly like what I see. But I also understand why some people are annoyed or at least confused. The challenge here is what the new edition is intended to be. I think with V5 and what we have seen about W5 the philosophy of the new editions seems to be to streamline the rules and setting, reset the metaplot in a way that makes it easier for new players to get into the setting without all the accumulated story and lore from 30 years of the game, and to borrow elements from the NwoD/CoD line. Some people seem to just not like that at all but I think if you want a full-on continuation of the original game then WoD20 is for you and not the WoD5 line. The issue here, for what it's worth, is that there is no H20 it's not as clear what this game is an update of. It's not an update of Hunter the Reckoning because it's about mortal hunters and not Imbued as was the original. And it's not really an</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">update of Hunters Hunted because it focuses exclusively from a player perspective on non-org hunters. So on it's own terms I think there's a lot of good in this game but I also think they missed the opportunity to either provide a new take on the Imbued or to provide a broader set of options for mortal hunters including more detailed options for playing as part of orgs (a did Hunter the Vigil). Honestly I think it would have been better if they'd genuinely taken the idea of HtV and ported it over to WoD5 ie rules for playing mortal hunters from street level to hunter orgs like the Inquisition, Arcanum etc. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T13:28:56-07:00","id":1488390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488360#post1488360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The challenge here is what the new edition is intended to be. I think with V5 and what we have seen about W5 the philosophy of the new editions seems to be to streamline the rules and setting, reset the metaplot in a way that makes it easier for new players to get into the setting without all the accumulated story and lore from 30 years of the game, and to borrow elements from the NwoD/CoD line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a disconnect because the nWW and Paradox teams have never stated most of this.<br /> <br /> Streamlining is certainly a goal, but there's been plenty of debate over how much streamlining has really happened vs. just shifting where the systems are clunky (or just streamline the rules and put more work on the ST to make up for it instead of actually having a more streamlined process).<br /> <br /> The metaplot is explicitly not reset, but continued. Sure there's a bit of retconning (just like every other edition). However V5 assumes in broadstrokes that everything in the previous editions happened as the books say that they happened. Just more stuff happened between 2003 and 2021. Nothing indicates that W5 is having a reset either instead of using the massive gap in time to put in all sorts of new metaplot material to get from 2003 to the new &quot;now&quot; Paradox wants. This point is particularly galling because the Driven are a brand new thing, the Imbued are ignored, and the orgs are pushed aside to make room for the Driven after formerly being treated as underdog mortals fighting against much more powerful supernatural forces and humanity's unknowing submission to supernatural control instead of being jobbers.<br /> <br /> That then impedes new players coming into the games. It's a fifth edition of a long running game line. People, even brand new players, are going to expect there to be a lot of stuff fans of the last four editions know about the game that they don't.... it would be kinda weird if that wasn't the case (even in D&amp;D once you're playing in existing settings like Forgotten Realms there's lore and metaplot to know). There's a big difference between trying to make the lore more accessible (which V5 has some good moves on doing) and just shunting off lots of lore so the new players know it exists but don't know what it is (something V5 also does, and H5 does instead of trying to have lore at all).<br /> <br /> And, while WoD5 does seem to be borrowing liberally from the CofD for design ideas, lets not leave out the other games they borrow from that they don't own. Which isn't a bad thing (that's how RPGs evolve) but it is generally good form to acknowledge when systems are lifted from other games rather than make it sound like the newest game to use them made them up themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some people seem to just not like that at all but I think if you want a full-on continuation of the original game then WoD20 is for you and not the WoD5 line. </div> </div> </div>This is unfair. The WoD5 line <b>is a continuation</b> of the previous editions. The 20th books are largely just omnibus collections with a bit of refinement of the previous three editions. The 20th books didn't continue the setting or plots. They're adamantly compatible with being used with any of the eras of the original run of the games by including rules for before and after various rules-impacting metaplot events. V20 covers things like Clans changing Disciplines (Dementation vs. Dominate Malks) and weaknesses (Banu Hakim and the Curse) so you can play before an event and through it with the attendant changes, ignore the event and keep the older method, or after the event with the post-event rules.<br /> <br /> If I want to see what happened to vampires after 2003, my options are V5, fan works on STV, or making it up myself. V20 doesn't do that.<br /> <br /> As I frequently point out, a lot of us that where around when Rich and Eddy announced their own new edition for VtM before the Paradox acquisition of the IP, were all really excited about it. VtM needed a proper new edition badly. Why a lot of us don't like V5 is because of what V5 turned out to be, not because V20 is what we really wanted all along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue here, for what it's worth, is that there is no H20 it's not as clear what this game is an update of. </div> </div> </div>It's not an update of anything. It's a new thing using an old name.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T17:10:04-07:00","id":1488414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488390#post1488390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's a disconnect because the nWW and Paradox teams have never stated most of this.<br /> <br /> Streamlining is certainly a goal, but there's been plenty of debate over how much streamlining has really happened vs. just shifting where the systems are clunky (or just streamline the rules and put more work on the ST to make up for it instead of actually having a more streamlined process).<br /> <br /> The metaplot is explicitly not reset, but continued. Sure there's a bit of retconning (just like every other edition). However V5 assumes in broadstrokes that everything in the previous editions happened as the books say that they happened. Just more stuff happened between 2003 and 2021. Nothing indicates that W5 is having a reset either instead of using the massive gap in time to put in all sorts of new metaplot material to get from 2003 to the new &quot;now&quot; Paradox wants. </div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, aside from some old stuff getting stripped off, like Crinos-born and the attendant first tenet of the litany. Still, that'd be equivalent to having a less punishing system for acquiring Imbued-style Edges, not the skin swap that H5 is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T00:53:12-07:00","id":1488440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488390#post1488390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's a disconnect because the nWW and Paradox teams have never stated most of this.<br /> <br /> Streamlining is certainly a goal, but there's been plenty of debate over how much streamlining has really happened vs. just shifting where the systems are clunky (or just streamline the rules and put more work on the ST to make up for it instead of actually having a more streamlined process).<br /> <br /> The metaplot is explicitly not reset, but continued. Sure there's a bit of retconning (just like every other edition). However V5 assumes in broadstrokes that everything in the previous editions happened as the books say that they happened. Just more stuff happened between 2003 and 2021. Nothing indicates that W5 is having a reset either instead of using the massive gap in time to put in all sorts of new metaplot material to get from 2003 to the new &amp;quot;now&amp;quot; Paradox wants. This point is particularly galling because the Driven are a brand new thing, the Imbued are ignored, and the orgs are pushed aside to make room for the Driven after formerly being treated as underdog mortals fighting against much more powerful supernatural forces and humanity's unknowing submission to supernatural control instead of being jobbers.<br /> <br /> That then impedes new players coming into the games. It's a fifth edition of a long running game line. People, even brand new players, are going to expect there to be a lot of stuff fans of the last four editions know about the game that they don't.... it would be kinda weird if that wasn't the case (even in D&amp;D once you're playing in existing settings like Forgotten Realms there's lore and metaplot to know). There's a big difference between trying to make the lore more accessible (which V5 has some good moves on doing) and just shunting off lots of lore so the new players know it exists but don't know what it is (something V5 also does, and H5 does instead of trying to have lore at all).<br /> <br /> And, while WoD5 does seem to be borrowing liberally from the CofD for design ideas, lets not leave out the other games they borrow from that they don't own. Which isn't a bad thing (that's how RPGs evolve) but it is generally good form to acknowledge when systems are lifted from other games rather than make it sound like the newest game to use them made them up themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is unfair. The WoD5 line <b>is a continuation</b> of the previous editions. The 20th books are largely just omnibus collections with a bit of refinement of the previous three editions. The 20th books didn't continue the setting or plots. They're adamantly compatible with being used with any of the eras of the original run of the games by including rules for before and after various rules-impacting metaplot events. V20 covers things like Clans changing Disciplines (Dementation vs. Dominate Malks) and weaknesses (Banu Hakim and the Curse) so you can play before an event and through it with the attendant changes, ignore the event and keep the older method, or after the event with the post-event rules.<br /> <br /> If I want to see what happened to vampires after 2003, my options are V5, fan works on STV, or making it up myself. V20 doesn't do that.<br /> <br /> As I frequently point out, a lot of us that where around when Rich and Eddy announced their own new edition for VtM before the Paradox acquisition of the IP, were all really excited about it. VtM needed a proper new edition badly. Why a lot of us don't like V5 is because of what V5 turned out to be, not because V20 is what we really wanted all along.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not an update of anything. It's a new thing using an old name.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good summary. I would say that I was really excited for VIV, and there was palpable disappointment among many when V5 was suddenly announced and VIV died. <br /> <br /> VIV would have had an open development process, like the CoD second editions, as they had begun with their blogs on Humanity and Gehenna. This would, I think, have resulted in a more polished core book in the way VTR2e is more polished. (That doesn't mean it would have used the same system.)<br /> <br /> V5 had a truncated open development process and H5 has had none. Which implies future books won't have that either. And that's always more risky, in my eyes, with a gameline that has significant nostalgia appeal.<br /> <br /> If people can see the book as it's developing, and can input into the development, they have a greater sense of ownership and will be less surprised by the final result. That reduces the chance of edition wars and flops.<br /> <br /> I can see in the other thread that at least one person has bought the book expecting Imbued and was disappointed when that didn't happen. That's the sort of surprise you want to avoid, unless you want buyers to feel cheated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T02:25:27-07:00","id":1488443,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that open development isn't the same thing as doing large playtests or Onyx Path's method of using Kickstarter backers as additional feedback sources via early manuscript releases and early backer pdfs.<br /> <br /> Open dev was on it's way out before all the CofD 2e cores used it, as the devs that used it the most either left the CofD/OPP or soured on how useful it was as a tool compared to more traditional dev with open playtests and backer feedback.<br /> <br /> Something that has frustrated people a lot with V5 is that there was a massive playtest and it seemed like a lot of feedback from it was simply ignored (including things some V5 writers that have come on since seem to feel shouldn't have been ignored), on top of the last round of playtests being dropped to get the book out for Gen Con (extremely old fashioned thinking as &quot;releasing at Gen Con&quot; simply isn't the event it was back before digital distribution became common place. It seems like Paradox learned the exact wrong lesson from how V5's playtesting went and opted to simply avoid early feedback in any sense rather than find a way to get some of the benefits of open dev in a still close dev process.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T03:43:20-07:00","id":1488446,"title":"","content":"In general I feel that Paradox has learned a lot of wrong lessons in all this. I think one of the issues they have is that they still have old ascended fans captaining the lines and should probably give more freedom to new blood. Taking Achilli for the credibility and putting him in charge of everything - even the stuff he doesn't like or care for - wasn't the right move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T14:50:07-07:00","id":1488494,"title":"","content":"I never played hunter the reckoning, but I played hunter the vigil 2th edition (and love it). I read the new edition out of curiosity and to see what it could offer that vigil could not, and here lies my main problem: Hunter the reckoning 5th edition doesn't offer anything truly different. In fact, I believe that both in terms of system and setting, it offers less. That made realize a simple truth that some people have already pointed out: this is a game for new players that come from vampire 5th edition. In that respect, I think they accomplished their task with a game that is easy to play. The thing is that for those of us that have more experience, this game feels so...bland. There's nothing in the book that makes it stand out, nothing truly original when you compare it with similar games. So this begs the question, what are their long term plans with this game? Do they have any? Because this book feels to me like little more than a sourcebook for vampire 5th, a momentary distraction before people go back to play with their vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T18:25:49-07:00","id":1488634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488323#post1488323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you mind sharing what appeals to you about the book? Is there anything you'd like them to keep the same/change in future books?<br /> <br /> I think it will be useful in helping the H5-curious figure out whether the book is going to be right for them. I also, selfishly, want WoD books to do well and bring loads of new players in, because even if I don't like some of the stuff 5e does, it does mean we're more likely to keep seeing new books come out for our favourite games (and I am a sucker for buying books, even if I'll never use them).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it largely comes down to my group already being familiar with V5 and that H5 is so light on things like metaplot (it's a good way to switch gears from being monsters to hunting monsters while still retaining a sense of continuity, if that makes sense?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T01:55:21-07:00","id":1488677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488443#post1488443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that open development isn't the same thing as doing large playtests or Onyx Path's method of using Kickstarter backers as additional feedback sources via early manuscript releases and early backer pdfs.<br /> <br /> Open dev was on it's way out before all the CofD 2e cores used it, as the devs that used it the most either left the CofD/OPP or soured on how useful it was as a tool compared to more traditional dev with open playtests and backer feedback.<br /> <br /> Something that has frustrated people a lot with V5 is that there was a massive playtest and it seemed like a lot of feedback from it was simply ignored (including things some V5 writers that have come on since seem to feel shouldn't have been ignored), on top of the last round of playtests being dropped to get the book out for Gen Con (extremely old fashioned thinking as &amp;quot;releasing at Gen Con&amp;quot; simply isn't the event it was back before digital distribution became common place. It seems like Paradox learned the exact wrong lesson from how V5's playtesting went and opted to simply avoid early feedback in any sense rather than find a way to get some of the benefits of open dev in a still close dev process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're quite right. I remember the pre-alpha and alpha playtests, and that the follow up playtest was abandoned. <br /> <br /> I also remember that VIV (as it was styled at the GenCon panel where it was announced) had blogs on Gehenna and Humanity, which seemed to suggest a bit more community input. I would've appreciated that.<br /> <br /> So what I wanted from V5 was a similar engagement process to the one suggested by OPP, though a CoD-style process would have been the best. Another round of playtesting would also have gone a long way. <br /> <br /> E.g., I feel like making Hunger more like Drive/Desperation, thereby allowing it to cover bonuses like Blood Surge and Discipline dice pool bonuses as well as things like losing control, would have gone a long way. Those boosted rolls could have a higher risk of consequences.<br /> <br /> It would serve to make Hunger something both desirable and dangerous -- encouraging players to take active risks with drawbacks that emerge, in part, from choosing to take those risks (rather than occurring primarily randomly), which I think better encapsulates the whole 'Hunger as addiction/temptation' thing than Hunger which is solely a punishment.<br /> <br /> H5 iterating on the core V5 systems, making them clearer and so on, would have been very welcome and would have almost convinced me to buy it. I think H5 does do some of that, but also, as it's quite skimpy on rules in general, it doesn't so enough to make it worthwhile for me (and I like the Imbued, so the rest wouldn't have appealed anyway).<br /> <br /> I'm stuck in the position of wanting to like WoD5, not being able to, and then feeling very conflicted as a result. It reminds me of WFRP3e -- I really liked the idea of the game, with all those cool narrative dice, <br /> trackers, tokens and cards to put all the rules at your fingertips, but in practice, it just didn't quite work. It was too clever by half.<br /> <br /> One day, it'll happen. But it seems maybe not with 5th edition. Though I would be pleased to be proven wrong! A WoD5 core rulebook, like CoD's blue book, with a revised and finessed system, that follows through on the promise of streamlining without resorting to handwaving, would hugely popular, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T03:49:24-07:00","id":1488680,"title":"","content":"I am curious to see how the upcoming &quot;advanced rules,&quot; book that's been talked about by the Paradox team shapes up. It seems, to me, very necessary to build on the V5 core system as the much more action heavy W5 looms on the horizon. Considering we also have the more whimsical quests of Dreaming, and high concept of Mage, expanded rules seem like they're going to get really important really fast. V5's condescended combat might work for vampires overwhelming mortals, or the Driven quickly finding out if their plans were perfect or trash, but I get the feeling that they're not going to hold up to a PC pack of Garou taking on a pack of BSDs in terms of capturing the feel of WtA's more splatterpunk happy history. Likewise the systems seem like they'll cut struggles short before the creative twists of fae cantrips or awakening magic can really come into things.<br /> <br /> While it is positive to see signs that Paradox is trying to course correct here, it's still a big question as to if it's too late for V5 and H5 being as good as they could have been to push the WoD5 line to it's full potential.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T04:51:00-07:00","id":1488683,"title":"","content":"There's something else I want to get out of my chest.<br /> <br /> Why does hunter the reckoning 5th hate hunter organizations so much?<br /> <br /> I get the impression that they want to force player characters to play in small groups with no support (tier 1 playstyle in hunter the vigil). I'm not against this type of game, it goes very well if you want to emphasize the feelings of paranoia, isolation and the fact that you're alone against the horror, but why make this the only option? I don't see why being driven and being a part of a larger group has to be incompatible, and their explanation for it is pretty lame. Likewise, I just don't get why they felt like they had to make every hunter organization downright evil at worst and selfish at best. I would really like to see more nuanced hunter organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-19-2022, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T05:23:18-07:00","id":1488685,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is the only option. It is in HtR5, but my guess is they will build upon the &quot;orgs&quot; in future supplements and possibly VtM5 books. Not sure how in detail &quot;2nd Inquisition&quot; details these orgs as playable. Hunter's Hunted II for 20th-Edition also isn't that seasoned by today's standards, so this customers might already be satisfied.<br /> <br /> And, I feel, a this are non-org Hunters with this mechanics and this are org-hunters with those mechanics would have made the book a mess. I already hated the &quot;this are vampires with disciplines, and these are quasi-vampires with this mechanics&quot;-approach in VtM5.<br /> <br /> <br /> And sure, 5th editions are continuations of the games lines, but they are not that compatible anymore, due to changes in setting and mechanics. So, with the Storyteller's Vault, they might go a similar way as D&amp;D3.5 did with Pathfinder 1. Sure, the license agreement of the Storyteller's Vault is by far not the Open Game License early version - but still, if you are interested into particular game, you might find good additional material there. And sometimes stuff that seamlessly fits with the printed material, since it was material cut from books due to editorial decisions, time or word count constrains. And sometimes it is home breed material of lesser quality or material that doesn't fit your head canon. So, Storyteller's Vault, for me, is always a bit of grain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T05:56:40-07:00","id":1488687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488683#post1488683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something else I want to get out of my chest.<br /> <br /> Why does hunter the reckoning 5th hate hunter organizations so much?<br /> <br /> I get the impression that they want to force player characters to play in small groups with no support (tier 1 playstyle in hunter the vigil). I'm not against this type of game, it goes very well if you want to emphasize the feelings of paranoia, isolation and the fact that you're alone against the horror, but why make this the only option? I don't see being why being driven and being a part of a larger group has to be incompatible, and their explanation for it is pretty lame. Likewise, I just don't get why they felt like they had to make every hunter organization downright evil at worst and selfish at best. I would really like to see more nuanced hunter organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>We discussed that in the other thread, but the general partyline seems to be that any organization is corrupt by being organised and needs to fold towards funding and secret masters, and as such it's not worthy of the TRUE Drive that the proper Hunters have. It's a very weird &quot;all authority is evil and we must fight it&quot; vibe that's inherit in V5 as well with Go Anarch or be the Assholes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T17:06:41-07:00","id":1488747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488687#post1488687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We discussed that in the other thread, but the general partyline seems to be that any organization is corrupt by being organised and needs to fold towards funding and secret masters, and as such it's not worthy of the TRUE Drive that the proper Hunters have. It's a very weird &quot;all authority is evil and we must fight it&quot; vibe that's inherit in V5 as well with Go Anarch or be the Assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably doesn't help that anarchs are the authority in their own territory which makes the books attitude to authority come across as hypocritical and somewhat self defeating.<br /> <br /> Its probably worth noting the 2nd inquisition has to be ridiculously corrupt otherwise the hunters just look like amatuers, since they're historically a way bigger threat that than you and and the mystery machine crew. Which kinds of damns hunters with faint praise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-01-2022, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T01:50:13-07:00","id":1488773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488747#post1488747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably doesn't help that anarchs are the authority in their own territory which makes the books attitude to authority come across as hypocritical and somewhat self defeating.<br /> <br /> Its probably worth noting the 2nd inquisition has to be ridiculously corrupt otherwise the hunters just look like amatuers, since they're historically a way bigger threat that than you and and the mystery machine crew. Which kinds of damns hunters with faint praise.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's not just the Second Inquistion - they are not even listed in H5 - there is a dozen groups in that book ranging from paramilitary groups to the Arcanum and Orpheus, yet they are ALL BAD!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T01:55:43-07:00","id":1488774,"title":"","content":"One thing I found hilarious (not in a good way) was the art that despicted the hunters killing werewolves (that's right, fucking werewolves) in hand to hand combat, I never liked apocalypse but if they have been nerfed to the extent that a human could knife one to death in one on one combat than I will take it as a clue that the writers decided to kill the franchise, like seriously hunters are regular ass people with no powers now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T02:50:02-07:00","id":1488778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488774#post1488774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I found hilarious (not in a good way) was the art that depicted the hunters killing werewolves (that's right, fucking werewolves) in hand-to-hand combat, I never liked apocalypse but if they have been nerfed to the extent that a human could knife one to death in one on one combat than I will take it as a clue that the writers decided to kill the franchise, like seriously hunters are regular ass people with no powers now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it also annoys me to no end. Hunter the vigil constantly emphasizes the importance of cooperation and hunting in a group, since almost every supernatural being will make a meal out of regular humans if they go alone, even if they have access to endowments or supernatural skills. Hell, being a bunch of clueless joes with more guts than brain trying to cooperate and eliminate something they're clearly not prepared to deal with is one of my favorite hunter games. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:45:00-07:00","id":1488797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488778#post1488778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it also annoys me to no end. Hunter the vigil constantly emphasizes the importance of cooperation and hunting in a group, since almost every supernatural being will make a meal out of regular humans if they go alone, even if they have access to endowments or supernatural skills. Hell, being a bunch of clueless joes with more guts than brain trying to cooperate and eliminate something they're clearly not prepared to deal with is one of my favorite hunter games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One thing that sets Vigil apart from reckoning V5 (aside from being an all around better game) is the fact that the game makes no secret that humans are, one on one, inferior to monsters and shouldn't be hunting them, the games give you a system that let's you make your own horror to hunt, you really aren't supposed to take on the other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:45:12-07:00","id":1488798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488747#post1488747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably doesn't help that anarchs are the authority in their own territory which makes the books attitude to authority come across as hypocritical and somewhat self defeating.<br /> <br /> Its probably worth noting the 2nd inquisition has to be ridiculously corrupt otherwise the hunters just look like amatuers, since they're historically a way bigger threat that than you and and the mystery machine crew. Which kinds of damns hunters with faint praise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thats just plain silly. Sigmata may get cartoonish and preachy but at least it understand large scale organization has merits as well as flaws.<br /> <br /> Edit-although I'll conceed this could be irl frustration talking here. It's hard to understate how toxic and demoralising I've found this attitude irl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-02-2022, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:07:49-07:00","id":1488834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488680#post1488680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to see how the upcoming &quot;advanced rules,&quot; book that's been talked about by the Paradox team shapes up. It seems, to me, very necessary to build on the V5 core system as the much more action heavy W5 looms on the horizon. Considering we also have the more whimsical quests of Dreaming, and high concept of Mage, expanded rules seem like they're going to get really important really fast. V5's condescended combat might work for vampires overwhelming mortals, or the Driven quickly finding out if their plans were perfect or trash, but I get the feeling that they're not going to hold up to a PC pack of Garou taking on a pack of BSDs in terms of capturing the feel of WtA's more splatterpunk happy history. Likewise the systems seem like they'll cut struggles short before the creative twists of fae cantrips or awakening magic can really come into things.<br /> <br /> While it is positive to see signs that Paradox is trying to course correct here, it's still a big question as to if it's too late for V5 and H5 being as good as they could have been to push the WoD5 line to it's full potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry what is this &quot;advanced rules&quot; book? Is it the player guide Modiphius was supposed to publish a few years ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T13:09:58-07:00","id":1488875,"title":"","content":"It's a new product in the works that Justin mentioned recently. From the sound of it, it's supposed to cover a lot more of the fine detail rules that V5 (and thus H5)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T01:57:20-07:00","id":1488955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488875#post1488875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a new product in the works that Justin mentioned recently. From the sound of it, it's supposed to cover a lot more of the fine detail rules that V5 (and thus H5)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is weird, I don't remember white wolf ever doing anything like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T02:21:49-07:00","id":1488957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488955#post1488955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is weird, I don't remember white wolf ever doing anything like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we've had all kinds of Player's Guides that usually brought expanded rules and player options, so it's not that odd. And I vaguely remember it was supposed to be a Player's Guide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T03:20:32-07:00","id":1488959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1488957#post1488957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well we've had all kinds of Player's Guides that usually brought expanded rules and player options, so it's not that odd. And I vaguely remember it was supposed to be a Player's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know of the players guide, I don't remember a book in particular that gives advanced rules for the whole WoD unless I got it wrong and it's something vampire specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T06:03:33-07:00","id":1488960,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think it is Vampire specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T10:01:17-07:00","id":1488983,"title":"","content":"The oWoD didn't do it much, because it was basically impossible with the rules inconsistencies between the different game-lines; though there are a few examples (WoD: Combat). The CofD did it multiple times (even some before the CCP merger) based on the shared base-line rule set. If WoD5 makes sure to keep the base rules the same, then a more detailed system for conflicts is something that can easily exist as a cross-game supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T07:52:19-07:00","id":1494672,"title":"","content":"FYI: The advanced rules book is going to be a PDF of all the stuff in the V5 systems and drama chapter that didn't get into H5. So falling damage, more options for combat, and so on.<br /> <br /> There will be a separate V5 Players Guide, which is different from the WoD5 Advanced Rules PDF and the V5 Companion PDF. That is supposed to have the non-corebook clans all in one place and may even clean up some of the rules, but I doubt it'll add a huge amount of crunch, because WoD5 doesn't seem geared towards that playstyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T04:14:33-07:00","id":1494854,"title":"","content":"I came to this thread eager to see if the new Hunter was worth picking up, and what I'm getting is that it basically covers the kind of characters the CofD corebook does (i.e. normal people without the backing of a dedicated organisation). Which kind of sucks, I guess if I want supernatural hunters I should stick to Scion: Origin or pick up Vigil 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T07:45:37-07:00","id":1495118,"title":"","content":"So, the expanded-rules supplement for WOD5E <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-expanded-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\">just dropped</a>. And there's one section that seems very relevant to H5 called &quot;Preparedness&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing slows a story down more than a lengthy inventory scene in which players list every conceivable item or object they may need for a night\u2019s activities. The preparedness test avoids this scenario by allowing players to test during the session to see if they remembered to bring something along or pick it up earlier.<br /> <br /> Characters need not roll for signature items: Of course the Martial Hunter brought their pistol, the sneaky Nosferatu brought their lockpicks, and so forth. Everybody has the normal sorts of things people might have in their pockets: cellphone, pocket knife, pencil, or what-have-you. This test covers slightly outr\u00e9 or unusual things: rope, a shovel or other larger tools, extra burner phones. The less likely the item, the higher the Difficulty the Storyteller should set.<br /> <br /> The Attribute for a preparedness test is Intelligence; the Skill should relate to the item or its use in some way. Roll Intelligence + Firearms to have brought a silencer, or Intelligence + Craft to remember a wrench, or Intelligence + Occult to produce a tarot deck from the folds of your trench coat. Storytellers should ask for rolls only if failure is interesting, and preparedness is no exception. Is it worth a roll to see if the characters remembered to bring their tickets to the concert? Maybe not if they had nothing distracting them, but if they fled an overturned car after a high speed chase, did they grab them from the glove box? Would not having the tickets bring the story to an unsatisfying halt? </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's remind ourselves how H5 portrayed its Asset-Edges in the book with this example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Amineh possesses the Arsenal Edge, together with Team Requisition and Special Features Perks. At the start of a scene she wants to provide as many large-caliber handguns as possible to her cell, together with concealed cases. The test is a win with a margin of three. One success in the margin is required for the case, and the remaining two provide two additional handguns, each with their own case. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it feel like Preparedness is simply a better-written version of what the Asset-Edges in H5 are? But if you use Preparedness-rules, why would any player ever pick Asset-Edges...?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T13:46:13-07:00","id":1495140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495118#post1495118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the expanded-rules supplement for WOD5E <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-expanded-mechanics&amp;quot;]just</a> dropped[/URL]. And there's one section that seems very relevant to H5 called &amp;quot;Preparedness&amp;quot;:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, let's remind ourselves how H5 portrayed its Asset-Edges in the book with this example:<br /> <br /> <br /> Doesn't it feel like Preparedness is simply a better-written version of what the Asset-Edges in H5 are? But if you use Preparedness-rules, why would any player ever pick Asset-Edges...?</div> </div> </div> </div>100%<br /> <br /> The vast majority of Edges are actively inferior to just buying the Asset/Ability in another way.<br /> <br /> Yet another reason I suspect there was very little communication between writers and compromised oversight from the Developer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T13:53:24-07:00","id":1495141,"title":"","content":"The expanded rules supplement is......well, it's a thing that exists.<br /> <br /> Someone needs to explain to ParaWoD that there is more to building a gamist influenced dramatist game system than taking a simulationist system and stripping out explanatory passages and mechanics and increasing the randomness and swinginess of the die mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T12:50:00-07:00","id":1495179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495140#post1495140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 100%<br /> <br /> The vast majority of Edges are actively inferior to just buying the Asset/Ability in another way.<br /> <br /> Yet another reason I suspect there was very little communication between writers and compromised oversight from the Developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hearing Justin Achilli talk about how he designed H5 to be a heist-game you can kinda get what the point of Asset-Edges is but the execution was... flawed. And while this entry does go a long way in fixing the flaws of those Edges, it doesn't solve the problem. Barebones Asset-Edges without Perks with the rules-as-written do stuff this Preparedness-rule suggests you shouldn't make anyone roll for anyway... unless you get high-damage/-value stuff. And that distinction isn't acknowledged by rules-as-written in the H5-book. And this obviously encourages min-maxing. If it's Diff 4 anyway, why not go for the high-end stuff you could potentially acquire...?<br /> <br /> But who knows if any errata could fix the Asset-Edges... The approach is so wrong and so far removed from what they're supposed to do. I think any ST is better off writing their own version rather than tinkering with these Edges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T16:19:39-07:00","id":1495200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495179#post1495179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hearing Justin Achilli talk about how he designed H5 to be <b>a heist-game</b>...<br /> <b>A <i>Heist</i>-Game</b><br /> designed the sequel to Hunter: the Reckoning to be <b>A Heist-Game</b></div> </div> </div> </div><i>WHAT?!?</i><br /> <br /> They want to redesign a game based around being chosen again your will to live a life of hunting/being hunted by the various WoD boogymen that run the world...<br /> <br /> As a tabletop Heist game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T19:46:49-07:00","id":1495216,"title":"","content":"Heist game, in this sense, in more in what he intended for the game-play loop to be like. He wanted H5 to be like the Leverage RPG, or Blades in the Dark, in how you go through episodic conflicts. But you hunt monsters instead of (just) taking things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T03:34:01-07:00","id":1495230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495200#post1495200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>WHAT?!?</i><br /> <br /> They want to redesign a game based around being chosen again your will to live a life of hunting/being hunted by the various WoD boogymen that run the world...<br /> <br /> As a tabletop Heist game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like HeavyArms said, the idea was inspired by the Leverage TV show which often would set up scenes where through flashbacks some kind of plan or preparation is revealed. And that was Justin Achilli's inspiration for how the Edges work. But he also said that the Desperation/Danger-Track is inspired by the movie Aliens but additionally he wanted H5 to be less about confronting the Quarry and more about preparation/planning and interaction with Touchstones. The mechanics are often flawed and sometimes not present at all to support what he thinks the design-goals of H5 are supposed to be. Honestly, I would be really interested in seeing Justin Achilli be the ST for an H5 campaign because I wanna see how he thinks H5 is supposed to be played.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T19:44:58-07:00","id":1495296,"title":"","content":"The basic premise reminds me of the &quot;horror story of the week vs. procedural mystery detectives&quot; early seasons of Supernatural. It's not all that alien a framing for the monster hunter section of the urban fantasy genre. Dracula is in many ways a technothriller, and I've taken far more WoD inspiration from crime fiction and other indirect genre touchstones than I have for horror or urban fantasy directly, TBH.<br /> <br /> When I think of hunter character concepts, I think Vic Mackey, Mike Ehrmentraut, Parker, Dexter Morgan, Carl Kolchak, the Continental Op, etc. The core loop of a monster hunter game is basically either a mystery procedural or a heist, in terms of structure, usually both. This was true of Hunter classic; you had some shortcuts provided by Edges (especially in terms of monster detection) but you were basically doing the same work - investigation, planning, takedown, extract - as you do in H5. Which is the heist format.<br /> <br /> The rules do basically nothing to support this, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T07:30:42-07:00","id":1495312,"title":"","content":"That's what confuses me about the statment Justin made. I get the concept and the narrative loop, but there is no hook for that in the mechanics as they are provided in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T10:21:28-07:00","id":1495318,"title":"","content":"i'm honestly surprised at how much i like it (i didn't care for the original) and my group is excited to see how it plays in relation to our ongoing v5 campaign (and where those things will intersect) but there is quite a bit of it that feels, strangely and sadly, sort of... unfinished in a way that reminds me of how many video games are rushed to market with the idea that they'll be finished by way of dlc and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T12:44:46-07:00","id":1495324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495318#post1495318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm honestly surprised at how much i like it (i didn't care for the original) and my group is excited to see how it plays in relation to our ongoing v5 campaign (and where those things will intersect) but there is quite a bit of it that feels, strangely and sadly, sort of... unfinished in a way that reminds me of how many video games are rushed to market with the idea that they'll be finished by way of dlc and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you liked it, may I recommend Hunter the Vigil It hits a similar vibe, but has a lot more material and is much better rounded out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T13:07:33-07:00","id":1495325,"title":"","content":"Also I want to add that is common to see people mixing WoD and CoD in their settings.So, if you like to mix with V5 lore, you have no many problems.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or even use the rules for the big hunters tiers and make playable the H5 organization hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T00:46:31-07:00","id":1495346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495324#post1495324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you liked it, may I recommend Hunter the Vigil It hits a similar vibe, but has a lot more material and is much better rounded out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Vigil is awesome and less prescriptive than Reckoning <s>2e</s>. Even if sadly my print copy is still in the post (curse you Royal Mail!) Also more easily able to run a Reckoning 1e style game, the Imbued are definitely a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Which is another thing, Vigil 2e is a lot less prescriptive. It fully supports street level play with Cells, but allows you to scale up to regional, continental, and even global scales, with each move granting you more benefits at the cost of more red tape. It just feels like a better game all round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T01:12:25-07:00","id":1495348,"title":"","content":"The reason that right now I have no interest in playing H5 is that it just seems way too much work to make this game work on its own terms. Especially because the premise and how it's presented aren't that interesting to begin with. Stuff like the relationship between difficulty and the Danger-track. You go to the rules-section and Danger is never mentioned, you go to the back-half of the book and the section on the Danger-track and the antagonist-section mention using Danger to calculate difficulty multiple times. And when this is mentioned it isn't even consistent with how Danger is used. So one thing the ST has to do with this game is to sit down and think about what the Danger-track actually does. Because the game doesn't offer a consistent, systematic presentation of how to use it. There are a bunch of examples and then the game just shrugs saying &quot;You go figure it out.&quot;. And there are <i>so many</i> other monsterhunter games out there (one of them being Hunter the Vigil of course). So why bother with one whose mechanics aren't explained very well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T07:58:11-07:00","id":1495354,"title":"","content":"i have a few of the first edition 'hunter: the vigil' books and just got the second edition but mostly to incorporate into the h5 game my group is working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T14:58:08-07:00","id":1495374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495354#post1495354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i have a few of the first edition 'hunter: the vigil' books and just got the second edition but mostly to incorporate into the h5 game my group is working on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you really want to take on H5, what may be of interest to you is the <a href=\"https://renegadegamestudios.com/hunter-the-reckoning/\" target=\"_blank\">free material offered by Renegade</a> since the release of H5. Of course, it has to be said that none of it actually fixes any of the problems H5 has. But it's good to have some of those game-aids like for Skill-rolls.<br /> <br /> One important thing mentioned there is that it's assumed that when your dice-pool is double the difficulty the player gets to narrate what happens no questions asked. Of course in this case it neglects to take Desperation-dice into account. But then again, the same chart talking about determining difficulty also doesn't acknowledge the Danger-track. So it's not like this is the only time Hunter-specific mechanics are ignored. Deciding how to handle this is just another thing your ST will have to deal with.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I can't emphasize this enough: The Creeds aren't balanced. The players need to know how the Creed-fields actually work and how constrictive some are compared to others. I mean, Entrepreneurial is the worst one hands down. Especially the one thing they are supposed to use Desperation-dice for goes completely against what Asset-Edges do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T15:07:17-07:00","id":1495376,"title":"","content":"aye, that lack of balance with creeds is something that we've all found really appealing about it (especially given the richer role playing that can arise between them all.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T15:22:59-07:00","id":1495377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495376#post1495376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aye, that lack of balance with creeds is something that we've all found really appealing about it (especially given the richer role playing that can arise between them all.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, hey, at the end of the day, as long as you're having fun at the table it's fine.<br /> <br /> I would just say that the imbalance in this case is a detriment to the whole game. The issue is that the Entrepeneurial Creed gets way less chances to use Desperation dice than other Creeds. And with that come less chances to trigger Overreach (which raises the Danger-track outside of ST-events). And I think the Desperation/Danger-track dynamic is the best part of the game. So a Creed that is so limited in using Desperation-dice is a bit of an issue. Also, what that Creed is supposed to do (building and repairing stuff) comes into conflict with what Asset-Edges do.<br /> <br /> As for roleplaying... I mean, mechanically outside of Creed-Fields Creeds are irrelevant. I wish there were more weight to them to give them the kind of emphasis/weight playbooks in Blades In The Dark or PbtA have. But because of how it's designed, Creed is a limitation, a burden - unless you pick one of the Creeds that give you very broad opportunities to use Desperation-dice. And that's the imbalance.<br /> <br /> The only thing less well represented in H5 is Drive, of course. For all that talk about Hunters with Drive, that whole Drive-thing is just a punishment for rolling badly rather than a character-defining trait.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T14:37:16-07:00","id":1495495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495118#post1495118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the expanded-rules supplement for WOD5E <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-expanded-mechanics&amp;quot;]just</a> dropped[/URL]. And there's one section that seems very relevant to H5 called &amp;quot;Preparedness&amp;quot;:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, let's remind ourselves how H5 portrayed its Asset-Edges in the book with this example:<br /> <br /> <br /> Doesn't it feel like Preparedness is simply a better-written version of what the Asset-Edges in H5 are? But if you use Preparedness-rules, why would any player ever pick Asset-Edges...?</div> </div> </div> </div>My immediate house rule would be that Asset-Edges add dice to the Preparedness roll, or give you a number of free acquisitions per story. Or maybe even both (add the dice every time you roll, but you can also burn a dot for the rest of the story by taking the thing when you need it without rolling).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495376#post1495376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aye, that lack of balance with creeds is something that we've all found really appealing about it (especially given the richer role playing that can arise between them all.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like... an odd compliment for a game. But if it works for you, that's great! I don't think it would work for most people, though, because most people expect games to at least have an illusion of fairness.<br /> <br /> I could understand if the Creeds were asymmetrical (so you make up for narrower fields with other cool stuff only you can do). But that doesn't seem to be the aim, and it requires greater system mastery to make asymmetric rules work in the long-run anyway, or people fall out.<br /> <br /> For something this light, you want the rules to be perfectly shaped, so they fade into the background rather than nagging you when they produce unbalanced outcomes (IMO, at least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T15:50:46-07:00","id":1495497,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if, once you remove Edges from the equation, do you actually need Creeds? Actually did 1e even need them? It might have been better to give each Virtue three Edges at each level and let each player pick and choose their powerset without guidance.<br /> <br /> The big potential thing that 1e Creeds added was the potential for inter-party conflict. Several of the Creeds had clashing philosophies with Avengers and Redeemers being the most obvious. What do the new Creeds actually add to the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T18:49:58-07:00","id":1495507,"title":"","content":"&quot;Need&quot; is always a bit loaded of a question with game design. That said in 1e:<br /> <br /> 1) The Imbued were a new thing for the WoD, so some player hand-holding for how to make appropriate characters justifies them bit more and the Creed were more integral to the metaphyics<br /> <br /> 2) Creeds were supposed help judge how much Conviction go rewarded for hunts based on how the hunt's resolution matched with Creed.<br /> <br /> 3) The Creeds all got more things that made them more mechanically distinct in the Creedbooks.<br /> <br /> Creeds in 5e seem mostly to exist for #1's reasons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T20:05:54-07:00","id":1495509,"title":"","content":"In terms of fixing, it would already help a great deal to give the Creed-FIelds some consistency.<br /> <br /> Let's start with Faithful and Martial:<ul><li>Faithful: Any direct conflict (physical, social, or mental) with the supernatural while on the Hunt.</li> <li>Martial: Physical conflict while on the Hunt (which need not be with the quarry itself, or even the supernatural).</li> </ul><br /> Both are about conflict while on the Hunt and Faithful talks about any direct conflict with the supernatural (the bit about &quot;physical, social or mental&quot; can go because that's just a description of well, any roll, there are no rolls that are not physical, social or mental). But Martial restricts it to phyiscal conflict and calls out that the supernatural/Quarry don't need to be involved.<br /> But then you get Inquisitive:<ul><li>Inquisitives: Gaining information while on the Hunt, such as research, breaking and entering, and interrogation.</li> </ul><br /> Here the supernatural/Quarry isn't mentioned at all. And rather than go with the &quot;physical, social or mental&quot; nomenclature, three example tasks that fall under mental (research), physical (breaking and entering) and social (interrogation) are listed. So Inquisitives can add Desperation-Dice to any roll as long as it fulfills the goal of gaining information. But gaining information about what...? In context with the previous two, it makes it sound like Inquisitives can add Desperation-Dice which is about gaining information in general even if it's unrelated to the supernatural/Quarry. And even then, with Martial this was called out but here, it isn't talked about at all.<br /> And once again, the formula changes with Underground:<ul><li>Underground: Stealth and subterfuge in service of the Hunt.</li> </ul><br /> Physical, Social and Mental aren't mentioned, the relation to the supernatural/Quarry isn't mentioned but now it also isn't goal-oriented like Inquisitive, this time it's about methodology. And no examples like with Inquisitive are listed. Also, it's suddenly &quot;in service of the Hunt&quot; instead of &quot;while on the Hunt&quot;.<br /> But the most confusing is Entrepreneurial:<ul><li>Entrepreneurial: Building, inventing, augmenting, or repairing while on the Hunt.</li> </ul><br /> Okay, no mention of Physical, Mental or Social, no goal-oriented description, no examples of tasks... it's just verbs. Does this Creed allow to add Desperation-Dice to repair... relationships as well? Or to invent an excuse? Or to build a legal case against somebody? It's just verbs after all. Of course, in the context of the bigger write-up we can assume this is all in relation to technology but still...<br /> <br /> This is what I mean when I say that I personally have no desire to play this right now. The foundation of this game thanks to its shoddy writing is so flawed that you'll have to put in work to get this game to a working state.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T01:21:27-07:00","id":1495515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495509#post1495509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of fixing, it would already help a great deal to give the Creed-FIelds some consistency.<br /> <br /> Let's start with Faithful and Martial:<ul><li>Faithful: Any direct conflict (physical, social, or mental) with the supernatural while on the Hunt.</li> <li>Martial: Physical conflict while on the Hunt (which need not be with the quarry itself, or even the supernatural).</li> </ul><br /> Both are about conflict while on the Hunt and Faithful talks about any direct conflict with the supernatural (the bit about &amp;quot;physical, social or mental&amp;quot; can go because that's just a description of well, any roll, there are no rolls that are not physical, social or mental). But Martial restricts it to phyiscal conflict and calls out that the supernatural/Quarry don't need to be involved.<br /> But then you get Inquisitive:<ul><li>Inquisitives: Gaining information while on the Hunt, such as research, breaking and entering, and interrogation.</li> </ul><br /> Here the supernatural/Quarry isn't mentioned at all. And rather than go with the &amp;quot;physical, social or mental&amp;quot; nomenclature, three example tasks that fall under mental (research), physical (breaking and entering) and social (interrogation) are listed. So Inquisitives can add Desperation-Dice to any roll as long as it fulfills the goal of gaining information. But gaining information about what...? In context with the previous two, it makes it sound like Inquisitives can add Desperation-Dice which is about gaining information in general even if it's unrelated to the supernatural/Quarry. And even then, with Martial this was called out but here, it isn't talked about at all.<br /> And once again, the formula changes with Underground:<ul><li>Underground: Stealth and subterfuge in service of the Hunt.</li> </ul><br /> Physical, Social and Mental aren't mentioned, the relation to the supernatural/Quarry isn't mentioned but now it also isn't goal-oriented like Inquisitive, this time it's about methodology. And no examples like with Inquisitive are listed. Also, it's suddenly &amp;quot;in service of the Hunt&amp;quot; instead of &amp;quot;while on the Hunt&amp;quot;.<br /> But the most confusing is Entrepreneurial:<ul><li>Entrepreneurial: Building, inventing, augmenting, or repairing while on the Hunt.</li> </ul><br /> Okay, no mention of Physical, Mental or Social, no goal-oriented description, no examples of tasks... it's just verbs. Does this Creed allow to add Desperation-Dice to repair... relationships as well? Or to invent an excuse? Or to build a legal case against somebody? It's just verbs after all. Of course, in the context of the bigger write-up we can assume this is all in relation to technology but still...<br /> <br /> This is what I mean when I say that I personally have no desire to play this right now. The foundation of this game thanks to its shoddy writing is so flawed that you'll have to put in work to get this game to a working state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree with those saying that stripping out detail and context has been taken as simplifying the rules. The rules aren't actually that much simpler; they just aren't defined as well when they exist, and the rest of the time they just don't exist in the first place.<br /> <br /> Procurement rolls are the obvious example. The version in the advanced rules PDF is so much simpler. They should've started with that as the basic rule and then made the Asset Edges modify that rule by making it easier or obviating the need for a roll at all.<br /> <br /> There are also other things that annoy me a little, but are less serious, such as the refusal to explain why some rolls are Attribute + Skill and some are Attribute + Attribute, which CoD does really well. I have read CoD, so the rationale is clear to me, but I don't think most WoD players would have casually looked up VTR2e to see if they can make sense of V5 rules.<br /> <br /> And in the advanced rules document, they've also started complicating things by adding a new type of opposed roll -- doing passive defences that are just based on a Skill, rather than taking half or having a contest, as in the main rules. <br /> <br /> They don't ever call them passive defences or spell it out, so again, the decision behind the rulings is opaque, which actually makes it harder to run the game rules-lite. <br /> <br /> A quick guideline about the uses of each type of opposition would be great, in the same way that CoD talks about contests and resistances, and when to use them.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Contests: Use whenever two narratively important parties actively engage each other, such as in combat or a battle of wits. E.g., PC versus Big Bad.<br /> Take half: When two parties engage each other, but the opponent is a minor character and/or you want to speed up the resolution, take half of their dice pool. E.g., PC v trivial NPC.<br /> Passive: When one party is working against an unwitting or inactive opponent, use the opponent's Skill rating as the Difficulty instead of taking half. (You could also use Discipline, Advantage or Power stats for things too.) E.g., PC v an NPC who is unaware of their presence.<br /> <br /> Now you have a framework which helps you make rulings on the fly without needing to consult the book for which dice pool or difficulty to use each time. <br /> <br /> That seems to be the sort of thing WoD5 wants you to be able to do, but it doesn't give you the tools to actually do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T09:55:41-08:00","id":1496315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1495515#post1495515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I agree with those saying that stripping out detail and context has been taken as simplifying the rules. The rules aren't actually that much simpler; they just aren't defined as well when they exist, and the rest of the time they just don't exist in the first place.<br /> <br /> Procurement rolls are the obvious example. The version in the advanced rules PDF is so much simpler. They should've started with that as the basic rule and then made the Asset Edges modify that rule by making it easier or obviating the need for a roll at all.<br /> <br /> There are also other things that annoy me a little, but are less serious, such as the refusal to explain why some rolls are Attribute + Skill and some are Attribute + Attribute, which CoD does really well. I have read CoD, so the rationale is clear to me, but I don't think most WoD players would have casually looked up VTR2e to see if they can make sense of V5 rules.<br /> <br /> And in the advanced rules document, they've also started complicating things by adding a new type of opposed roll -- doing passive defences that are just based on a Skill, rather than taking half or having a contest, as in the main rules.<br /> <br /> They don't ever call them passive defences or spell it out, so again, the decision behind the rulings is opaque, which actually makes it harder to run the game rules-lite.<br /> <br /> A quick guideline about the uses of each type of opposition would be great, in the same way that CoD talks about contests and resistances, and when to use them.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Contests: Use whenever two narratively important parties actively engage each other, such as in combat or a battle of wits. E.g., PC versus Big Bad.<br /> Take half: When two parties engage each other, but the opponent is a minor character and/or you want to speed up the resolution, take half of their dice pool. E.g., PC v trivial NPC.<br /> Passive: When one party is working against an unwitting or inactive opponent, use the opponent's Skill rating as the Difficulty instead of taking half. (You could also use Discipline, Advantage or Power stats for things too.) E.g., PC v an NPC who is unaware of their presence.<br /> <br /> Now you have a framework which helps you make rulings on the fly without needing to consult the book for which dice pool or difficulty to use each time.<br /> <br /> That seems to be the sort of thing WoD5 wants you to be able to do, but it doesn't give you the tools to actually do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one aspect of H5 that is still mystifying to me is how Hunter-specific rules never seem to come into play when the book describes the general rules of the Storyteller-system. When you go on the Renegade-website and get their handouts for determining difficulty, resolving rolls etc., there's, for example, the advice that when you roll and your dicepool is twice as big as the difficulty you don't need to roll and instead the player gets to narrate what happens. The book barely touches on that as a mechanic and the Storytelling-chapter never deals with the idea of &quot;players as temporary Storytellers as result of a roll&quot; like any good story-game would. It's not just &quot;Hey, you have a critical success and now you get to do something awesome&quot;, but the ST sets a difficulty, the player takes a course of action and the applicable dicepool is so big, the player in question gets to narrate what happens from beginning to end in regards to the action. But here's the question: Do Desperation-Dice count for that...? Counting Desperation-Dice for that will have <i>huge</i> consequences for gameplay because of the mechanic I mentioned before (because Desperation-Dice are added to your dicepool thereby increasing the chance of player never having to roll at all and just narrating what happens instead).<br /> <br /> But it's <i>never </i>talked about in the H5 corebook.<br /> <br /> To date, there's not a single official piece of writing that can give you an answer to that.<br /> <br /> Same with the Danger-Track and difficulty. It's like the people who wrote about the general Storyteller-system rules in the H5 corebook didn't even know what the Hunter-specific rules were supposed to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T10:42:47-08:00","id":1496319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1496315#post1496315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same with the Danger-Track and difficulty. It's like the people who wrote about the general Storyteller-system rules in the H5 corebook didn't even know what the Hunter-specific rules were supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that probably is the case. If you hop on over to the W5 thread, you'll find reference to a Q&amp;A with Justin Achilli which suggests a lot of the Garou-specific rules are still undefined or TBD, despite the book being slated for 2023.<br /> <br /> I think what's happening is that the core WoD5 rules are being written first, and splat-specific rules are being finished later, so they have to be slotted in without much time to integrate the two sets of rules.<br /> <br /> This explains why H5 seems to have so many gaps. Things were just cut out instead of being developed. V5 had a bit of that going on, as well, but it was worse in Hunter. Then there's the lack of public playtest, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T11:21:40-08:00","id":1496323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1496319#post1496319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that probably is the case. If you hop on over to the W5 thread, you'll find reference to a Q&amp;A with Justin Achilli which suggests a lot of the Garou-specific rules are still undefined or TBD, despite the book being slated for 2023.<br /> <br /> I think what's happening is that the core WoD5 rules are being written first, and splat-specific rules are being finished later, so they have to be slotted in without much time to integrate the two sets of rules.<br /> <br /> This explains why H5 seems to have so many gaps. Things were just cut out instead of being developed. V5 had a bit of that going on, as well, but it was worse in Hunter. Then there's the lack of public playtest, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>What's so strange about this is that we're talking about basic stuff here. Also, the whole existence of the &quot;Expanded Rules&quot;-book as a &quot;living document&quot; (ie it gets regular updates) is a double-edged sword when looking at H5. When there's so little consideration in paying attention to the minutiae of the mechanics and how they impact the experience at the table, then what made H5 so bad will be an issue for all WOD5E games going forward. When there's an Expanded rules&quot;-book in existence that is considered optional, the idea of how the game is supposed to work in the creators' minds becomes much more complicated - both for the writers and the people who will eventually play the game. And then it's natural for authors to write with a perspective where they either just assume you know what they're getting at without providing clarity within the text or they're unaware of an issue with how the game works (especially because now there's a version of the game with expanded rules applied and one without those).<br /> <br /> Maybe it could work if Justin Achilli &amp; co had a good framework for their version of the WOD5E Storyteller system. But H5 clearly wasn't that.<br /> <br /> In regards to W5, since we're talking about the bad way H5 with rules... There's this part in the Discord-Q&amp;A where I had flashbacks to when Justin Achilli talked about &quot;sober play&quot; and why H5 didn't need a morality-system (similar to Humanity in V5):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Will 'Chronicle Tenets' feature in W5? If yes, will they be a gameplay-element like in V5 or more of a mix of gameplay and 'Safety Tool' as in H5 (which I think has some problems)?</b><br /> Still in development. Werewolf has a lot of &quot;moving parts&quot; systemically, and the more systems in place, the more of a challenge to uninfluenced play there are. Werewolves don't have Convictions, for example, for that very reason, while the tribes have Ban and Favor suggesting key attitudes and values. </div> </div> </div>I can't wait for W5 to have the same dissonance as H5 has... In H5 you're supposed to play the &quot;good hunters&quot;, not those cheap knockoffs who work for organizations. And if your hunter-player-character cares absolutely nothing about collateral damage and starts with three Touchstones but only starts caring after two of them die, the system provided in the book is absolutely fine with that. Justin Achilli really seems to believe that game-systems are a hindrance to play. That doesn't mean all games need to be these huge tomes of rules and mechanics (like Shadowrun, for example) but in my opinion the big issue is that Justin Achilli wants a pure Story-game and the WOD5E-Storyteller-system as established by V5 isn't that. And since this is a game as a brand which still wants to uphold V5 as part of the brand, he can't just flip the table and start over completely. But he still has these nagging thoughts in his head like that systems are a hurdle to playing the game.<br /> <br /> And that's the whole rationale for &quot;sober play&quot; and removing the &quot;Humanity-morality-system: In Justin's mind Humanity is a system that makes it harder for players to do what they want - and that's bad. The solution: Don't have that system. I don't think that's a solution. Also, good story-games like good PbtA-games may be rules-light but what systems they have matters. The idea of rules-light isn't for the system to stay out of the way, it's for the system to emphasize and focus on what matters thematically to the game and the kind of storytelling it wants to emphasize.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T00:34:06-08:00","id":1496378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488136-hunter-the-reconing-5th-edition?p=1496323#post1496323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's so strange about this is that we're talking about basic stuff here. Also, the whole existence of the &amp;quot;Expanded Rules&amp;quot;-book as a &amp;quot;living document&amp;quot; (ie it gets regular updates) is a double-edged sword when looking at H5. When there's so little consideration in paying attention to the minutiae of the mechanics and how they impact the experience at the table, then what made H5 so bad will be an issue for all WOD5E games going forward. When there's an Expanded rules&amp;quot;-book in existence that is considered optional, the idea of how the game is supposed to work in the creators' minds becomes much more complicated - both for the writers and the people who will eventually play the game. And then it's natural for authors to write with a perspective where they either just assume you know what they're getting at without providing clarity within the text or they're unaware of an issue with how the game works (especially because now there's a version of the game with expanded rules applied and one without those).<br /> <br /> Maybe it could work if Justin Achilli &amp; co had a good framework for their version of the WOD5E Storyteller system. But H5 clearly wasn't that.<br /> <br /> In regards to W5, since we're talking about the bad way H5 with rules... There's this part in the Discord-Q&amp;A where I had flashbacks to when Justin Achilli talked about &amp;quot;sober play&amp;quot; and why H5 didn't need a morality-system (similar to Humanity in V5):<br /> <br /> <br /> I can't wait for W5 to have the same dissonance as H5 has... In H5 you're supposed to play the &amp;quot;good hunters&amp;quot;, not those cheap knockoffs who work for organizations. And if your hunter-player-character cares absolutely nothing about collateral damage and starts with three Touchstones but only starts caring after two of them die, the system provided in the book is absolutely fine with that. Justin Achilli really seems to believe that game-systems are a hindrance to play. That doesn't mean all games need to be these huge tomes of rules and mechanics (like Shadowrun, for example) but in my opinion the big issue is that Justin Achilli wants a pure Story-game and the WOD5E-Storyteller-system as established by V5 isn't that. And since this is a game as a brand which still wants to uphold V5 as part of the brand, he can't just flip the table and start over completely. But he still has these nagging thoughts in his head like that systems are a hurdle to playing the game.<br /> <br /> And that's the whole rationale for &amp;quot;sober play&amp;quot; and removing the &amp;quot;Humanity-morality-system: In Justin's mind Humanity is a system that makes it harder for players to do what they want - and that's bad. The solution: Don't have that system. I don't think that's a solution. Also, good story-games like good PbtA-games may be rules-light but what systems they have matters. The idea of rules-light isn't for the system to stay out of the way, it's for the system to emphasize and focus on what matters thematically to the game and the kind of storytelling it wants to emphasize.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it sort of flies in the face of the other overriding message of WoD5 games: that games must always be played a certain way (e.g., no org Hunters, no Sabbat vampires, etc). So it's all a bit muddled. If you want to insist people only play a certain way, Touchstones and Convictions actually make sense.<br /> <br /> I can only assume that someone saw the critiques of Touchstones, Convictions and Chronicle Tenets in V5 and got scared of making those count for anything in games going forward, rather than recognising what the problem was and working to address it. Again, the solution was to remove a system rather than clarify or refine it.<br /> <br /> For example, HTV2e gets to build upon all the lessons learned since VTR2e. Instead of 10 levels of breaking points, it only has three (much easier to manage) with innate and Code breaking points (this factors in personal/hunter morals despite having a generic Integrity system).<br /> <br /> HTV2e's system would've been perfect for V5. You have three broad sets of innate breaking points/sins based on your connection to your mortal life, plus some personal triggers that could represent your individual ethics (or even those of a Path). Touchstones wouldn't need to be human in that system, because the ties to humanity are already embedded in your, well, Humanity trait.<br /> <br /> H5 could've done something similar and allowed them to better explore the tension they wanted to create between being a righteous avenger in desperate circumstances (the Hunters) and organising/selling out to better fight that evil (hunters in orgs). <br /> <br /> Touchstones would therefore be the things that remind you why you fight, while your Integrity would be the balance between either standing alone and becoming more desperate, or joining with others and running the risk of becoming compromised. <br /> <br /> The increasing desperation of going it alone could provide more Desperation Dice to get you through based on sheer fear, paranoia and adrenaline, while those with org backing could become softer and more comfortable, and thus less able to use Desperation but more able to rely on better resources instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}